.TITLE "uname"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Prints detailed information about the system and the Linux kernel. it helps you identify the __architecture__, __kernel version__, and __operating system__ type.

.DIV "TLDR"
**uname**
Displays the name of the operating system kernel (e.g., Linux).
> 

**uname -a**
Displays all available system information in a single line.
> __-a__ all information flag

**uname -r**
Displays the current kernel release version.
> __-r__ kernel release flag

**uname -m**
Displays the machine hardware architecture (e.g., x86_64).
> __-m__ machine architecture flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __uname -a__ is a standard first step when troubleshooting system compatibility issues. It provides the essential context needed to download the correct drivers or software packages for your specific hardware and kernel.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:hostnamectl** **linux:lsb_release** **linux:uptime**

